<style>
body { font-family: 'Calibri', 'Segoe UI', Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; color: #1a1a1a; margin: 1in; }
h1 { font-size: 22pt; color: #003366; border-bottom: 2px solid #003366; padding-bottom: 4px; margin-top: 18pt; }
h2 { font-size: 14pt; color: #004080; border-bottom: 1px solid #ccc; padding-bottom: 3px; margin-top: 14pt; }
table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 12pt 0; }
th, td { border: 1px solid #bbbbbb; padding: 6pt 8pt; text-align: left; }
th { background-color: #f0f4f8; font-weight: bold; color: #003366; }
pre, code { font-family: 'Consolas', 'Courier New', monospace; background-color: #f5f5f5; font-size: 9.5pt; }
pre { padding: 8pt; border: 1px solid #ddd; white-space: pre-wrap; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Organization-Scoped Skill Registry Vertical Slice</h1>
<h2>1. Overview & Core Guarantees</h2>
<p>This service provides an organization-scoped registry where enterprise organizations (such as ABC Construction and XYZ Builders) can draft, review, version, and activate AI COO operational skills without risk of cross-tenant data leakage or silent in-place prompt mutation.</p>
<p>Core Architectural Guarantees:<br>- Canonical Ownership Boundary: All entities are strictly keyed by organization_id. Cross-tenant queries are blocked and audited.<br>- Skill Lifecycle: State transitions strictly follow draft -> active -> disabled.<br>- Immutable Versioning: An active skill cannot be mutated in place. Any update produces an incremented immutable snapshot (v1, v2, ...).<br>- Role-Based Activation: Only organization owner roles can activate skills. Duplicate activation requests are safe and idempotent.<br>- Tool Sandboxing: Requested tools are validated against an approved registry. Destructive primitives (delete_database, execute_shell, format_disk, etc.) are rejected with explicit HTTP 422 errors.<br>- Auditability: An append-only audit trail records every draft creation, version addition, activation, disablement, and cross-tenant access violation.<br>- Dual Database Architecture: Target production runs on PostgreSQL (Docker Compose); zero-dependency local evaluation runs on SQLite with enforced foreign key pragmas.</p>
<h2>2. Pre-Seeded Fixture Organizations</h2>
<table><thead><tr><th>Organization</th><th>ID</th><th>Fixture Users</th><th>Roles</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>ABC Construction</td><td>org_abc</td><td>alice_owner, bob_member</td><td>owner, member (Field Engineer)</td></tr><tr><td>XYZ Builders</td><td>org_xyz</td><td>carol_owner, dan_member</td><td>owner, member (Project Manager)</td></tr></tbody></table>
<h2>3. Quickstart & Deployment</h2>
<p>Option A: Docker Compose (PostgreSQL Stack)<br>1. Copy environment template: cp .env.example .env<br>2. Build and launch: docker-compose up --build -d<br>3. Verify health: curl http://localhost:8000/health</p>
<p>Option B: Local Zero-Config Evaluation (SQLite)<br>1. Install dependencies: pip install -r requirements.txt<br>2. Run server: uvicorn app.main:app --port 8000<br>3. Open Swagger UI at http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs</p>
<h2>4. Running Automated Tests</h2>
<pre>pytest -v tests/</pre>
<h2>5. End-to-End Workflow API Examples</h2>
<p>Step 1: Create a Skill Draft (Member or Owner)<br>POST /api/v1/skills with headers: X-Organization-Id: org_abc, X-User-Id: bob_member, X-User-Role: member</p>
<p>Step 2: Read Skill & Version History<br>GET /api/v1/skills/{id}</p>
<p>Step 3: Owner Activation (Idempotent)<br>POST /api/v1/skills/{id}/activate with headers: X-User-Role: owner</p>
<p>Step 4: Department Runtime Retrieval<br>GET /api/v1/skills/runtime/department/operations</p>
<p>Step 5: Audit Trail Verification<br>GET /api/v1/audit-logs?resource_id={id}</p>
</body></html>